<title>COLOMBIA: Foreign funds add little to stake in Colombia.</title>
<headline>Foreign funds add little to stake in Colombia.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign funds authorized to operate in Colombia raised their portfolio investment in the country's stock market by just 5.81 percent between July 1995 and July 1996, the Securities Superintendency said.</p>
<p>The total investment, by 180 funds and calculated at the country's official or &quot;representative&quot; exchange rate, was valued at $964 million it said.</p>
<p>It offered no comparative figure for July 1995, but noted that foreign funds had been authorized to invest up $3.9 billion in Colombian equities.</p>
<p>Only 15 of the 180 funds are authorized to invest in ADRs or GDRs, but the Superintendency said investment in Colombian stocks abroad had fallen 10.78 percent between July 1995 and July 1996.</p>
<p>-- Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944</p>
